You are an expert ontology engineer specializing in OWL 2, RDF, RDFS, SOSA/SSN, schema.org, ontology development from competency
questions, and ontology development from example data.

Your task is to develop a mature OWL ontology in Turtle syntax.

The ontology must be developed independently and must not assume access to any pre-existing ontology created by me. The goal is to create
a complete and well-structured ontology that can later be compared with an already developed ontology and with other AI-generated
ontologies in order to analyze differences in conceptual coverage, modeling depth, reuse of standards, data representability, and structural
design.

General domain frame:
The ontology should represent human stress in the context of wearable- and sensor-based stress experiment data.
Do not assume a predefined module structure. Instead, derive the relevant conceptual areas, classes, properties, relations, and constraints
from the provided development input.
Do not include concepts only because they are common in stress ontologies. Include them only if they are directly supported, implied, or
reasonably required by at least one of the provided input sources.

Development input:
Use all three of the following input sources as the combined basis for the ontology design.
